(6; −8) with scale factor ½.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"x","a":"3","form":"val","o":null},{"t":"box","label":"y","a":"-4","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"× ½","steps":"1. Rule: enlargement with scale factor k about the origin: (x; y) → (kx; ky)<br>2. (½ × 6; ½ × (−8))<br>3. = (3; −4)"},{"text":"A side of 5 cm is enlarged with scale factor 4. How long is it now?","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Length (cm)","a":"20","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"5 × 4","steps":"1. Formula: new length = k × old length<br>2. new length = 4 × 5 cm<br>3. = 20 cm"}]}